---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import { withBase } from "../lib/paths";
---

<Layout
  title="About Muse"
  description="A personal software collection, made with care and AI assistance. Meet the idea behind Muse."
  current="about"
>
  <div class="container page-content">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">A little introduction</p>
      <h1>
        Small ideas.
        <br />
        <span>Thoughtfully made.</span>
      </h1>
      <p>
        Muse is a personal collection of software projects, each starting with a
        simple idea: make an everyday task a little better.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <section class="about-story" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
        <h2 id="about-heading">Independent by nature.</h2>
        <p>
          Muse is an independent personal project, not a company. It’s a place
          for useful tools with focused purposes and considered interfaces.
        </p>
        <p>
          AI tools help with designing and building the projects. Those tools
          may change over time; Muse is not tied to any one model or provider.
          The projects and their source repositories remain the source of truth.
        </p>
        <p>
          The aim is simple: software that does something useful, feels pleasant
          to use, and respects the person using it.
        </p>
        <a class="button button-filled" href={withBase("software/")}>
          Explore the collection <Icon name="arrow" size={20} />
        </a>
      </section>
      <aside class="about-principles" aria-label="What guides Muse">
        <p class="eyebrow">What guides the work</p>
        <div>
          <Icon name="heart" />
          <h3>Purpose before more.</h3>
          <p>
            A clear job to do. No features just for the sake of a longer list.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <Icon name="layers" />
          <h3>Different Apps. One Muse.</h3>
          <p>
            Individual tools, connected by a shared, accessible design language.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <Icon name="code" />
          <h3>Tools can change.</h3>
          <p>
            AI-assisted development, with project knowledge kept in the
            repository.
          </p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
